{"p": "P represents the statistical significance of the comparison between two sets of data, indicating the probability that the observed difference could have occurred by chance.|Here is another description: P represents the statistical significance level in the context of comparing the performance of random forest and logistic regression models in predicting outcomes after transplantation."},
{"p_____0_04": "The predicate '=' indicates that the value of P is exactly 0.04, suggesting a statistically significant result at a conventional threshold (typically P < 0.05)."},
