{"0_835_0_831_0_840": "The object \"0.835 [0.831\u20130.840]\" represents the ANN AUC value with a 95% confidence interval, indicating the accuracy of the ANN model in predicting graft failure at 1 month post-transplant."},
{"donor_risk_index_auc": "The Donor risk index AUC is a measure of the accuracy of the Donor risk index in predicting outcomes, specifically early graft survival in liver transplant recipients."},
{"donor_risk_index_auc__was__0_680_0_669_0_690": "The predicate 'was' indicates the specific value or result obtained for the Donor risk index AUC in the context of the study, reflecting its performance in predicting graft failure at 1 month."},
{"0_680_0_669_0_690": "The value 0.680 [0.669\u20130.690] represents the area under the curve (AUC) for the Donor risk index, showing its accuracy in predicting graft failure, with a 95% confidence interval ranging from 0.669 to 0.690."},
{"soft_score_auc": "The SOFT score AUC is a measure of the accuracy of the SOFT score in predicting outcomes, specifically graft failure at 1 month post-transplant in liver transplant (LT) recipients."},
