{"ml_based_models__were__more_accurate_than_commonly_adopted_scores": "The predicate \"were\" indicates a past comparison or evaluation of the ML-based models against other methods. It suggests that the models have been assessed and found to have certain characteristics or performance metrics in relation to other established methods."},
{"more_accurate_than_commonly_adopted_scores": "Commonly adopted scores in the context of liver transplantation refer to traditional scoring systems used to predict outcomes such as graft survival. These scores are typically derived from logistic regression analyses and include metrics like the Donor risk index and SOFT score, which are based on a set of predefined variables."},
{"gain": "The gain refers to the improvement or advantage obtained from using machine learning (ML) models over traditional methods for predicting graft and patient survival in liver transplantation."},
{"gain__was_often__not_clinically_relevant": "The phrase \"was often\" indicates a frequent occurrence or common trend observed in the context of using ML models for prediction. It suggests that the described situation or outcome happened regularly or consistently."},
{"not_clinically_relevant": "The term \"not clinically relevant\" describes a situation where the improvement or advantage provided by ML models, compared to traditional methods, did not have a significant impact on clinical decision-making or patient outcomes in the context of liver transplantation."},
{"model_by_lau_et_al": "The model by Lau et al. is a machine learning-based model designed to predict graft failure in liver transplant recipients. It was developed using data from deceased donor liver transplant recipients transplanted between 2010 and 2015."},
{"model_by_lau_et_al__provided__less_accurate_prediction_for_90_day_outcome": "The predicate \"provided\" indicates that the model by Lau et al. was used to generate predictions for the 90-day outcome of liver transplant recipients. This usage highlights the model's application in a specific context to forecast patient outcomes."},
{"less_accurate_prediction_for_90_day_outcome": "The less accurate prediction for the 90-day outcome refers to the model's performance when applied to predict graft failure at 90 days post-transplant. Despite showing good accuracy for predicting graft failure at 1 month, the model's accuracy decreased when the prediction endpoint was extended to 90 days."},
{"random_forests_auc": "Random forests AUC refers to the area under the curve (AUC) metric derived from a machine learning model known as random forests. This metric is used to evaluate the performance of the model in predicting outcomes, such as graft failure in liver transplant recipients."},
{"random_forests_auc__was__0_715_0_705_0_724": "The predicate \"was\" indicates that the random forests AUC value is a recorded or measured outcome from a specific study or analysis. It signifies that the AUC value of 0.715 (0.705\u20130.724) was obtained as a result of applying the random forests model to predict 90-day graft failure in liver transplant recipients."},
{"0_715_0_705_0_724": "The object \"0.715 (0.705\u20130.724)\" represents the AUC value achieved by the random forests model in predicting 90-day graft failure. This value, along with its 95% confidence interval, indicates the accuracy of the model in distinguishing between graft failures and non-failures within the studied population of liver transplant recipients."},
{"ann_auc__was__0_559_0_548_0_569": "The predicate \"was\" indicates that the ANN AUC value is a recorded measurement or result from a specific study or analysis, reflecting the performance of the ANN model at a particular point in time."},
{"0_559_0_548_0_569": "The object \"0.559 (0.548\u20130.569)\" represents the ANN AUC value with a 95% confidence interval, indicating the accuracy of the ANN model in predicting 90-day outcomes for liver transplant recipients, as reported in the study by Lau et al."},
{"ml__will_presumably_be__a_useful_tool_for_improving_organ_allocation_and_predicting_short_term_graft_and_patient_survival": "\"Will presumably be\" indicates a future expectation based on current trends and evidence. In this context, it suggests that based on existing studies and the performance of ML models, there is an anticipation that ML will play a significant role in the field of liver transplantation."},
{"a_useful_tool_for_improving_organ_allocation_and_predicting_short_term_graft_and_patient_survival": "A useful tool for improving organ allocation and predicting short-term graft and patient survival refers to the potential applications of ML in enhancing the efficiency and accuracy of liver transplantation processes. This includes better matching of donor organs to recipients and more precise predictions of post-transplant outcomes."},
{"available_studies": "The available studies refer to research and analyses conducted on liver transplant (LT) recipients, focusing on the application of machine learning (ML) for predicting graft and patient survival. These studies encompass a range of methodologies and variables to assess the accuracy of ML models in comparison to traditional scoring systems."},
{"available_studies__provided_information_on__patients_transplanted_over_a_broad_period_of_time_with_different_liver_disease_etiologies_and_involving_different_donors": "The phrase \"provided information on\" indicates that the available studies have yielded data and insights regarding the performance and applicability of ML models in predicting outcomes for liver transplant patients. This information is crucial for understanding the potential benefits and limitations of using ML in this context."},
{"patients_transplanted_over_a_broad_period_of_time_with_different_liver_disease_etiologies_and_involving_different_donors": "The object \"patients transplanted over a broad period of time, with different liver disease etiologies and involving different donors\" describes the diverse group of liver transplant recipients studied. These patients vary in the time of their transplantation, the underlying causes of their liver diseases, and the characteristics of their donors, reflecting a comprehensive dataset that aims to capture the complexity of liver transplantation outcomes."},
{"applicability_of_ml_based_prognostics": "The applicability of ML-based prognostics refers to the potential use and effectiveness of machine learning models in predicting outcomes for liver transplant (LT) recipients. These models aim to improve the accuracy of predictions over traditional scoring systems."},
{"applicability_of_ml_based_prognostics__remains_to_be_seen__for_current_or_future_lt_cohorts": "The phrase \"remains to be seen\" indicates that the effectiveness or applicability of ML-based prognostics in the context of liver transplantation is yet to be determined or confirmed through further research and validation."},
{"for_current_or_future_lt_cohorts": "Current or future LT cohorts refer to the groups of liver transplant recipients, either those who have recently undergone transplantation or those who will undergo transplantation in the future. These cohorts are the target population for applying ML-based prognostic models to assess their outcomes."},
{"long_term_outcome_after_solid_organ_transplantation": "Long-term outcome after solid organ transplantation refers to the health status and survival of patients who have undergone organ transplant surgery over an extended period. This includes the functionality of the transplanted organ and the overall well-being of the patient.|Here is another description: The long-term outcome after solid organ transplantation refers to the health and functionality of the patient and the transplanted organ over an extended period following the transplant procedure."},
{"long_term_outcome_after_solid_organ_transplantation__is_difficult_to_predict__even_more_than_in_the_early_posttransplant_period": "The phrase \"is difficult to predict\" indicates the challenge in forecasting the long-term results of solid organ transplantation. This unpredictability arises from various factors that can influence the patient's health post-transplant."},
{"even_more_than_in_the_early_posttransplant_period": "The phrase \"even more than in the early posttransplant period\" highlights that predicting long-term outcomes is more challenging compared to the initial period following the transplant. This is due to additional factors such as infections, malignancies, and metabolic or cardiovascular diseases that can affect the patient's health over time."},
{"long_term_outcome_after_solid_organ_transplantation__may_be_influenced_by__conditions_unrelated_to_the_graft": "The phrase \"may be influenced by\" indicates a potential impact or effect on the long-term outcome after solid organ transplantation, suggesting that various factors could play a role in determining the success and health of the patient post-transplant."},
{"conditions_unrelated_to_the_graft": "Conditions unrelated to the graft include a range of health issues that are not directly connected to the transplanted organ itself, such as infections, malignancies, and metabolic or cardiovascular diseases, which can nonetheless significantly affect the overall long-term outcome of the transplantation.|Here is another description: Conditions unrelated to the graft refer to various health issues that can affect a patient's long-term outcome after solid organ transplantation, independent of the transplanted organ itself.|Here is another description: Conditions unrelated to the graft refer to various health issues that can affect a patient after solid organ transplantation, independent of the transplanted organ itself.|Here is another description: Conditions unrelated to the graft refer to various health issues that can affect a patient's long-term outcome after solid organ transplantation, independent of the transplanted organ's function."},
