{"patients__underwent__lt": "The predicate \"underwent\" indicates that the patients in the study experienced or were subjected to a particular medical procedure as part of their treatment and evaluation process."},
{"lt": "LT, or Liver Transplantation, is the medical procedure that the patients underwent. It involves replacing a diseased liver with a healthy one from a donor, and in this study, it was used to assess long-term outcomes in patients.|Here is another description: LT, or liver transplantation, is a surgical procedure where a diseased or failed liver is replaced with a healthy liver from a donor. It is a critical treatment option for patients with end-stage liver disease or acute liver failure."},
