{"living_donor_lt": "The object \"living donor LT\" stands for living donor liver transplantation, a surgical procedure where a portion of the liver is transplanted from a living donor to a recipient. In this study, it represents the specific type of liver transplant performed on a subset of the patient population."},
{"cases_of_living_donor_lt": "Cases of living donor liver transplantation (LT) refer to instances where a portion of the liver is donated by a living individual to be transplanted into a recipient. This type of transplantation is a critical procedure in addressing severe liver conditions where a deceased donor organ is not immediately available."},
