{"ml_model__afforded__accurate_prognosis_on_patient_survival_between_1_and_5_years_after_lt": "The term 'afforded' in this context signifies that the ML model provided or enabled the capability to make an accurate prognosis. It indicates the model's effectiveness in delivering a reliable prediction based on the analyzed data."},
{"accurate_prognosis_on_patient_survival_between_1_and_5_years_after_lt": "An accurate prognosis on patient survival between 1 and 5 years after LT refers to the ML model's ability to predict with high reliability the likelihood of a patient's survival within this timeframe post-transplantation, based on various input factors and data patterns."},
{"auc_standard_error": "The AUC (standard error) is a statistical measure used to evaluate the performance of a model, particularly in the context of predicting outcomes such as patient survival after liver transplantation (LT). It represents the area under the receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve, which illustrates the trade-off between sensitivity and specificity."},
{"auc_standard_error__was__0_864_0_043": "The predicate \"was\" indicates that the AUC (standard error) value of 0.864 (0.043) is a recorded or observed measurement in the context of evaluating the prognosis model's accuracy for patient survival after liver transplantation."},
