{"cold_ischemia_time": "Cold ischemia time refers to the duration that an organ, such as a kidney, remains preserved in a cold environment before transplantation. This period is critical as it can affect the organ's viability and function post-transplant."},
{"cold_ischemia_time__and__intraoperative_mixed_venous_oxygen_saturation": "The conjunction \"and\" in this context signifies that both cold ischemia time and intraoperative mixed venous oxygen saturation are equally important factors that influence the outcome of renal dysfunction post-transplant."},
{"intraoperative_mixed_venous_oxygen_saturation": "Intraoperative mixed venous oxygen saturation is a measure of the oxygen level in the blood returning to the heart from the body's tissues during surgery. It is an indicator of the body's overall oxygenation status and can impact the success of organ transplantation."},
{"cold_ischemia_time_and_intraoperative_mixed_venous_oxygen_saturation": "Cold ischemia time refers to the period during which an organ, such as a kidney, is kept at a low temperature to preserve its function before transplantation. Intraoperative mixed venous oxygen saturation is a measure of the oxygen level in the blood returning to the heart from the body's tissues during surgery, which can indicate the adequacy of tissue perfusion and oxygen delivery."},
{"cold_ischemia_time_and_intraoperative_mixed_venous_oxygen_saturation__were__the_most_important_variables_associated_with_renal_dysfunction": "The predicate \"were\" signifies that the subject elements, cold ischemia time and intraoperative mixed venous oxygen saturation, have been identified as having a specific characteristic or role. In this context, it indicates that these two factors have been determined to be significant in relation to the object."},
{"the_most_important_variables_associated_with_renal_dysfunction": "Renal dysfunction refers to the impaired functioning of the kidneys, which can manifest as a reduced ability to filter waste products from the blood, regulate fluid and electrolyte balance, and produce hormones that control blood pressure and red blood cell production. In the context of transplantation, renal dysfunction can be a critical complication affecting patient outcomes."},
{"study": "The study refers to a research project that explored the probability of new-onset diabetes after liver transplantation (LT) in a large cohort of patients from the US transplant registry. It utilized a high-performance random forest model to predict diabetes outcomes post-transplant.|Here is another description: The study refers to a research effort conducted by Bhat et al. that utilized a high-performance random forest model to analyze a large cohort of patients from the US transplant registry."},
