{"differences__were_between__the_two_cohorts_baseline_characteristics": "The phrase \"were between\" indicates the existence of a gap or distinction in characteristics when comparing the two cohorts. It suggests that the differences are situated within the baseline characteristics of these groups, highlighting the contrast or variance that exists between them."},
{"the_two_cohorts_baseline_characteristics": "The two cohorts\u2019 baseline characteristics refer to the initial set of attributes, features, or conditions that define each cohort at the beginning of a study or observation period. These characteristics could include various factors such as demographic information, health status, or other relevant metrics that are measured before any interventions or treatments are applied."},
