{"models__exhibited__good_accuracy_in_predicting_graft_failure_at_1_month": "The predicate \"exhibited\" indicates that the models demonstrated or showed a certain level of performance in their intended task, which in this context is the prediction of graft failure."},
{"good_accuracy_in_predicting_graft_failure_at_1_month": "Good accuracy in predicting graft failure at 1 month refers to the models' ability to correctly forecast the occurrence of graft failure within the first month post-transplantation, as measured by area under the curve (AUC) values close to 1, indicating high predictive accuracy."},
{"random_forest_auc": "The random forest AUC refers to the area under the curve (AUC) metric derived from a random forest model, which is a machine learning technique used for classification and regression tasks. In this context, it is used to evaluate the accuracy of predicting graft failure in liver transplant recipients."},
{"random_forest_auc__was__0_818_0_812_0_824": "The predicate \"was\" indicates that the random forest AUC value is a recorded measurement or result from the study. It signifies that the random forest model's performance, as measured by the AUC, was quantified and found to be a specific value within a given confidence interval."},
{"0_818_0_812_0_824": "The object \"0.818 [0.812\u20130.824]\" represents the specific value of the random forest AUC, along with its 95% confidence interval. This value indicates the accuracy of the random forest model in predicting graft failure at 1 month post-transplant, with the confidence interval providing a range within which the true AUC is likely to fall."},
{"ann_auc": "ANN AUC refers to the Area Under the Curve (AUC) of a Receiver Operating Characteristic (ROC) curve for an Artificial Neural Network (ANN) model. In the context of liver transplantation, it measures the model's ability to distinguish between graft failures and successes.|Here is another description: ANN AUC refers to the Area Under the Curve (AUC) of a model using Artificial Neural Networks (ANN) to predict outcomes, in this case, early graft survival in liver transplant recipients."},
