{"soft_score_auc": "The SOFT score AUC is a measure of the accuracy of the SOFT score in predicting graft failure at 1 month post-transplant. It is one of the models evaluated in the context of liver transplantation (LT) outcomes."},
{"soft_score_auc__was__0_638_0_632_0_645": "The predicate \"was\" indicates the recorded value or result of the SOFT score AUC in the study. It signifies that the SOFT score AUC had a specific value within a given confidence interval."},
{"0_638_0_632_0_645": "The object \"0.638 [0.632\u20130.645]\" represents the Area Under the Curve (AUC) value of the SOFT score, which is a statistical measure used to evaluate the performance of a diagnostic test. The value of 0.638 indicates the accuracy of the SOFT score in predicting graft failure, with a 95% confidence interval ranging from 0.632 to 0.645."},
{"ml_based_models__were_more_accurate_than__commonly_adopted_scores": "The phrase \"were more accurate than\" indicates a comparative evaluation between ML-based models and other methods, highlighting the superior performance of the former in terms of prediction accuracy."},
{"commonly_adopted_scores": "Commonly adopted scores in the context of liver transplantation refer to established statistical methods or scoring systems, such as the Donor Risk Index and SOFT score, which are traditionally used to assess and predict graft and patient survival outcomes."},
{"ml_based_models__provided__less_accurate_prediction_for_90_day_outcome": "The predicate \"provided\" indicates that the ML-based models were utilized to generate predictions. In this specific context, it highlights the outcome of applying these models to forecast the 90-day survival of liver grafts post-transplantation."},
{"less_accurate_prediction_for_90_day_outcome": "The object \"less accurate prediction for 90-day outcome\" describes the result of using ML-based models to predict the survival of liver grafts 90 days after transplantation. It suggests that while these models are effective for short-term predictions, their accuracy diminishes when predicting longer-term outcomes like the 90-day survival rate."},
{"random_forests_auc": "Random forests AUC refers to the area under the curve (AUC) metric obtained from a machine learning model known as random forests. This metric is used to evaluate the performance of the model in predicting a specific outcome, in this case, early graft survival in liver transplant (LT) recipients."},
{"random_forests_auc__was__0_715_0_705_0_724": "The predicate \"was\" indicates that the random forests AUC value is a recorded result or outcome from a specific study or analysis. It signifies that the mentioned AUC value was achieved by the random forests model in predicting the 90-day graft failure endpoint."},
{"0_715_0_705_0_724": "The object \"0.715 (0.705\u20130.724)\" represents the AUC value obtained by the random forests model in predicting the 90-day graft failure endpoint. This value, along with its 95% confidence interval (CI), indicates the accuracy or performance of the model in making predictions for this specific outcome."},
