{"one_year_after_lt": "One year after LT refers to the time frame starting from the date of liver transplantation and extending for a year. This period is crucial for evaluating the initial recovery and adaptation of the transplanted liver, as well as the overall health of the patient post-surgery."},
{"patients": "The patients in this context are individuals who have been part of a study involving liver transplantation. Specifically, they are over 2 years old and were included in a research project that aimed to predict long-term outcomes post-transplantation.|Here is another description: The patients in this context are individuals who have undergone liver transplantation (LT) and are part of a study analyzing long-term outcomes using an ANN-based model. They represent a specific demographic within the study, focusing on those who received the transplant."},
{"patients__underwent__lt": "The predicate \"underwent\" signifies that the patients in the study experienced or were subjected to a specific medical procedure. In this case, it refers to the patients having undergone liver transplantation as part of their treatment."},
{"lt": "Liver transplantation (LT) is a surgical procedure where a diseased or failing liver is replaced with a healthy liver from a donor. In the context provided, LT is the critical medical intervention that the patients underwent, and its outcomes are being studied to predict long-term results.|Here is another description: Liver transplantation (LT) is a surgical procedure involving the replacement of a diseased liver with a healthy liver from a donor. It is often considered for patients with end-stage liver disease or acute liver failure."},
{"patients__were__2_years_old": "The predicate \"were\" in this context signifies the state or condition of the patients at the time of the liver transplantation. It indicates that the patients met a specific criterion, which is being over two years old, at the time they underwent the procedure."},
{"2_years_old": "The object \">2 years old\" describes the age criterion for the patients included in the study. It specifies that all patients in the study were older than two years at the time of their liver transplantation, which is a critical factor for the analysis of long-term outcomes using the ANN-based model."},
