{"cases__were__living_donor_lt": "The predicate \"were\" indicates the proportion or percentage of the total patient group that falls under the category of living donor liver transplantations."},
{"living_donor_lt": "Living donor LT refers to a type of liver transplantation where a portion of the liver is donated by a living person, as opposed to a deceased donor. This method is used to provide a life-saving organ to a recipient in need."},
{"cases_of_living_donor_lt": "Cases of living donor liver transplantation (LT) refer to instances where a portion of the liver is donated by a living individual to be transplanted into a recipient. This type of transplantation is a critical procedure in addressing severe liver conditions where deceased donor organs are not immediately available."},
{"cases_of_living_donor_lt__were__10_7": "The predicate \"were\" indicates the proportion or percentage that the cases of living donor LT represent within the total number of liver transplantations performed during the specified period. It establishes a quantitative relationship between the subject and the object."},
{"10_7": "10.7% represents the proportion of liver transplantations that were living donor cases out of the total number of liver transplantations performed on patients over two years old between 2008 and 2013. This percentage highlights the prevalence of living donor liver transplantations within the overall transplantation activities during that time frame."},
